WEBVTT

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:27.460
Japan  11:57 PM

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:18.490
It's finally over today, huh?

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:22.870
It wasn't any different 
than it always is, though.

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:25.170
You've got that right.

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:34.590
Wait, is this real?

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:40.990
Everybody, look at this.

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:43.490
Is this...

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:45.070
No way...

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:48.190
I can't believe it!

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:51.000
Wait, where is this happening?

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:54.760
America!

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:14.650
New York, United States of America
10:57 AM

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:34.560
It's okay now, ma'am.

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:55.890
There they are.

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:46.010
<i>Emma! Emma!</i>

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:48.510
<i>What's going on out there?</i>

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:49.950
<i>Emma!</i>

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:56.650
<i>We're not getting audio?</i>

00:05:57.410 --> 00:06:00.580
<i>It seems that something's 
happened at the third</i>

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:03.320
<i>anniversary memorial ceremony held 
in Times Square, New York today.</i>

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:04.090
<i>Can you hear me?</i>

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:06.170
<i>Can the studio hear me?</i>

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:06.970
<i>Emma!</i>

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:08.300
<i>Are we live?</i>

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:13.140
<i>I'm here at Times Square, where the 
memorial ceremony was being held,</i>

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:16.980
<i>when a terrorist holding what 
appeared to be a flamethrower—</i>

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:21.270
<i>Are you okay, Emma?</i>

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:24.450
<i>First, get yourself to safety!</i>

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:25.860
<i>Get somewhere safe!</i>

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:27.990
<i>Wow...</i>

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:30.610
<i>How do I even describe this?</i>

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:34.660
<i>I suppose you could call them... monsters.</i>

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:41.210
<i>There are two monsters that look</i>

00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:43.000
like an ugly frog and a bat,

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:46.300
and one that looks like something right 
off the pages of a comic book...

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:48.590
Some kind of robot...

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:50.590
Wow.

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:35.300
Ribbit! Ribbit! Ribbit!

00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:47.020
Ribbit!

00:08:08.660 --> 00:08:09.590
Ribbit!

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:38.700
I'd originally been prepared to be 
your producer, and make you a star.

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:42.200
Well, even if the stands are empty,

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:47.290
if we can heat things up here, 
the audience will surely notice.

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:15.070
More.

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:17.740
Scream, so that more people come.

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:22.700
Start screaming, miserably and loudly, 
that you're going to die.

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:38.760
What was that?

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:52.190
Stupid brat...

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:58.110
Let's head towards the audience.

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:29.560
I'll just have you scream instead.

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:36.190
He took mine, too?

00:11:56.510 --> 00:11:58.010
The Russian ninja?

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:03.600
Make it fast.

00:12:20.910 --> 00:12:22.590
I didn't hear anything about this.

00:12:22.890 --> 00:12:26.350
He's pretty bulky to be your partner, but...

00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:30.900
At least let me tell you "good job."

00:12:31.580 --> 00:12:33.400
That's the problem with freelancers.

00:12:53.970 --> 00:13:55.560
"Sky Show"! "Sky Show"! "Sky Show"!

00:13:29.810 --> 00:13:31.180
Ultrasonic waves...

00:13:31.180 --> 00:13:32.890
Must be that bat-face.

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:35.340
I guess he's what you'd expect, at least.

00:14:03.060 --> 00:14:05.940
This is the end, blue guy.

00:14:04.580 --> 00:14:13.200
"Sky Show"! "Sky Show"! "Sky Show"!

00:14:54.150 --> 00:14:58.070
This is your first time. It's only 
natural that you'd be surprised.

00:14:58.610 --> 00:15:00.920
But this is now our case.

00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:03.670
Are you from the FBI?

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:04.950
We're above them.

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:09.140
If you have any complaints, 
take them up with DC.

00:15:15.150 --> 00:15:18.310
Um... First of all, who are you?

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:19.430
Are you a robot?

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:22.310
I'm...

00:15:22.310 --> 00:15:23.320
You can talk!

00:15:23.680 --> 00:15:24.690
I'm me.

00:15:25.930 --> 00:15:31.010
Is this some kind of special suit 
that you're, um... wearing?

00:15:33.900 --> 00:15:37.400
Right, well... Please tell us your name.

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:40.280
Me?

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:41.750
I'm...

00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:49.330
Guy?

00:15:53.370 --> 00:15:55.360
I... I-Guy!

00:16:01.150 --> 00:16:16.830
I-Guy! I-Guy! I-Guy!

00:16:03.010 --> 00:16:04.460
The interview's over.

00:16:05.990 --> 00:16:07.740
I-Guy, one last thing!

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:11.480
You'll continue to protect New York, right?

00:16:13.600 --> 00:16:16.300
Sorry. I actually live in LA.

00:16:21.740 --> 00:16:25.800
<i>I-Guy! I-Guy! I-Guy!</i>

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:31.500
<i>Um, I wonder why the 80s hit 
song "Sky Show" is playing...</i>

00:16:34.190 --> 00:16:35.150
Wait!

00:16:49.380 --> 00:16:50.470
Ugh!

00:17:17.100 --> 00:17:20.500
Huh... I guess the rumors were true.

00:17:21.030 --> 00:17:24.000
You guys taking us to Area whatever?

00:17:25.830 --> 00:17:27.660
You can't be serious.

00:17:27.660 --> 00:17:30.390
I'm not an alien!

00:17:30.390 --> 00:17:32.720
Huh? I'm close enough?

00:17:32.720 --> 00:17:35.290
You don't hold back, do ya? I'm hurt.

00:17:35.290 --> 00:17:36.150
Shut up.

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:39.930
Oh, come on. We'll be parting soon enough.

00:17:39.930 --> 00:17:41.290
Oops, I let it slip.

00:17:42.220 --> 00:17:43.500
Oh, well.

00:17:44.190 --> 00:17:49.160
Say, do you know why I'm so calm right now?

00:17:49.640 --> 00:17:52.730
He's going to come and save us soon.

00:17:52.730 --> 00:17:55.460
Wrai— Our buddy.

00:17:57.230 --> 00:17:58.290
And here he comes.

00:18:17.050 --> 00:18:21.280
I told you not to get ahead 
of yourself, you scum!

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:24.390
Same goes for you.

00:18:24.390 --> 00:18:25.110
Ribbit?

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:31.180
<i>Cage 2 to Cage 1!</i>

00:18:31.180 --> 00:18:35.050
<i>The Reflected we were transporting 
have disappeared. All of them!</i>

00:18:58.680 --> 00:19:01.540
Steel Ruler, I am terribly sorry.

00:19:02.240 --> 00:19:04.020
Those fools...

00:19:04.020 --> 00:19:08.110
We didn't anticipate such enthusiasm 
for the man with the mohawk.

00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:12.670
There's another emotion hidden 
beneath their enthusiasm.

00:19:13.360 --> 00:19:17.020
When we, the Reflected, who are 
unsightly and possess strange powers,

00:19:17.020 --> 00:19:19.630
were being pitifully and 
pathetically defeated,

00:19:20.010 --> 00:19:22.490
the people were shouting for joy.

00:19:23.550 --> 00:19:25.710
One might say a very exclusive attitude

00:19:25.710 --> 00:19:29.250
toward us has been growing, 
undetected, over the past three years.

00:19:32.780 --> 00:19:34.650
Our leader's plan

00:19:36.020 --> 00:19:40.050
has finally taken a great step forward.

00:19:50.160 --> 00:19:53.580
Baltimore, Maryland

00:20:36.240 --> 00:20:43.620
<i>So it can be said that New York 
was saved by the hero named I-Guy.</i>

00:20:44.150 --> 00:20:45.310
<i>However,</i>

00:20:45.310 --> 00:20:49.360
<i>I'd like to assert that this 
all happened because of the</i>

00:20:49.360 --> 00:20:53.080
<i>Reflection incident that impacted 
the world three years ago.</i>

00:20:53.080 --> 00:20:54.400
<i>Let's hear more about that.</i>

00:20:54.870 --> 00:20:59.420
<i>Three years ago, our world 
was struck by a catastrophe.</i>

00:20:59.420 --> 00:21:02.990
<i>We were hit by that smoke and that light...</i>

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:06.420
<i>But we still don't know why it occurred.</i>

00:21:06.420 --> 00:21:07.240
<i>Right.</i>

00:21:07.900 --> 00:21:12.950
<i>Meanwhile, many have completely 
recovered, seemingly with no problems.</i>

00:21:12.950 --> 00:21:15.750
<i>But I've heard that some of those people</i>

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:20.750
<i>are recently suffering 
from various side effects.</i>

00:21:21.410 --> 00:21:24.350
<i>So what is it that you're trying to say?</i>

00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:27.470
<i>I don't want to make claims 
based on speculation,</i>

00:21:28.430 --> 00:21:31.430
<i>but this wasn't just some terrorist attack.</i>

00:21:31.970 --> 00:21:34.440
<i>I believe the effects of 
the Reflection incident</i>

00:21:34.770 --> 00:21:39.360
<i>unfortunately manifested in 
the form of today's events.</i>

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:41.280
<i>Oh, come on. You can't be serious.</i>

00:21:41.660 --> 00:21:46.020
<i>It's like you're implying those 
monsters were the Reflected.</i>

00:21:46.020 --> 00:21:48.050
<i>That's not what I said.</i>

00:21:48.450 --> 00:21:52.060
<i>More importantly, I believe 
there's a bigger problem</i>

00:21:52.060 --> 00:21:56.070
<i>with the term "Reflected" that you 
just used to describe them.</i>

00:21:56.390 --> 00:21:59.080
<i>That's a discriminatory thing to say.</i>

00:21:59.080 --> 00:22:01.330
<i>Don't change the subject.</i>

00:22:08.750 --> 00:22:10.070
X-On...

00:22:12.880 --> 00:22:14.000
Say...

00:22:17.890 --> 00:22:20.800
Did I do something to upset you?

00:22:27.220 --> 00:22:29.290
<i>That day three years ago...</i>

00:22:46.240 --> 00:22:50.370
<i>It wasn't something that 
affected everyone equally.</i>

00:22:53.330 --> 00:22:54.870
<i>We...</i>

00:22:59.270 --> 00:23:00.980
<i>were chosen.</i>

00:24:45.000 --> 00:24:55.010
Next Time 
Survivor

00:24:48.170 --> 00:24:55.010
Narration: Stan Lee
